id: pm-beads-yk8k
title: Declaring the pm CLI as a runtime dependency gives consumers a second nested copy whenever their host pin differs
description: "This package declared @unbrained/pm-cli in both dependencies and peerDependencies. The two ranges were separately satisfiable, so npm resolved them independently: a consumer installing the CLI at 2026.8.3, which satisfies this package's own declared peer floor, received the host copy at 2026.8.3 plus a nested 2026.8.13 under node_modules of this package. npm dedupes only when the ranges happen to overlap, so the tree is clean for some host pins and skewed for others. Skew matters here because consecutive CLI releases disagree about whether identical history bytes are fatal, a warning, or invisible, so which copy loads can decide a workspace gate verdict. The package is a pure extension with no bin entry, and sixteen sibling packages import the same SDK at runtime while declaring it only as a peer plus dev dependency."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: correctness,packaging
created_at: "2026-08-13T21:12:53.995Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T21:15:20.215Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-13T21:15:20.197Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-13T21:15:20.197Z"
author: codex
expected_result: Installing this package alongside any CLI version its declared peer range admits yields exactly one resolvable @unbrained/pm-cli.
actual_result: "Before the change, installing the CLI at 2026.8.3 with this package yielded two copies: the host at 2026.8.3 and a nested 2026.8.13. After it, the packed tarball installed into a clean project resolves one copy at 2026.8.13 and imports successfully with every export intact."
files[4]{path,scope,note}:
  .gitattributes,project,merge-driver fence regenerated to the v2 form the pinned CLI writes
  package-lock.json,project,resolves a single CLI copy at 2026.8.13
  package.json,project,pm CLI moved out of dependencies and the dev pin made exact
  test/packaging.test.ts,project,manifest guard proven to fail against the previous shape
tests[2]{command,path,scope}:
  "name=the host CLI is declared as a peer dependency and never as a runtime dependency,result=pass",test/packaging.test.ts,project
  "name=the host CLI dev dependency is pinned to an exact version rather than a range,result=pass",test/packaging.test.ts,project
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1003",project,upstream request for host-side detection of two resolvable CLI copies
close_reason: "Removed @unbrained/pm-cli from dependencies, leaving the peer declaration the host satisfies, and pinned the dev declaration exactly to 2026.8.13. Verified by packing the tarball and installing it into a clean project alongside the CLI: one resolvable copy, and the extension imports with every export intact. A manifest guard in test/packaging.test.ts pins both properties and was proven to fail against the previous shape."
body: ""
